Data Flow Specification1. Brush Geometry & CSG to JMS PipelineThe pipeline transforms unconstrained user brush volumes into a strictly indexed, single-node or multi-node Blam! Jointed Model Skeleton (.JMS) file.+------------------+      +---------------------+      +------------------------+      +-------------------+
|  CSG Half-Edge   | ---> | Triangular Splitting| ---> |   Material Semantic    | ---> | JMS Node & Face   |
|  Primitives (B-Rep)     |  & Planar Weld      |      |   Prefix Resolver      |      | Serializer (v8290)|
+------------------+      +---------------------+      +------------------------+      +-------------------+
Step 1: Geometry NormalizationCoordinate Conversion: Convert right-handed Y-up (standard DCC space) to Blam! standard: Right-handed Z-up ($X = \text{Forward}$, $Y = \text{Left}$, $Z = \text{Up}$), scaled by engine world units ($1\text{ World Unit} \approx 10\text{ feet} = 3.048\text{ meters}$).Convex Decomposition: Non-convex brushes are split into convex components using an internal BSP splitter to guarantee valid lightmap unwrapping and collision generation during tool execution.Weld Phase: Vertices sharing identical spatial coordinates ($E = 1 \times 10^{-5}$) are collapsed, but split when smoothing groups or UV seams diverge.Step 2: Halo Material Semantic EncodingMaterials mapped to faces in the editor assign physical properties using Blam! prefix tags before writing out the material list in the JMS stream:PrefixEngine InterpretationExample Applied Material<none>Renderable surface with collisionconcrete_wall!Render-only (no collision)!glass_decorative~Collision-only (invisible geometry)~invis_barrier%Two-sided lighting evaluation%leaf_canopy*Skybox projection*sky_dome+Special markers (ladder, portal, exact)+ladder_rungStep 3: JMS v8290 Specification StreamingThe pipeline formats text directly into the standard JMS version string (Halo 2/Halo 3 baseline):8290
